---
name: scljet-mutation-complete-parse
description: SclJet SQL mutations consume their complete token stream before returning a new image
backends: [int, js]
---

# scljet — mutation parsers fail closed

Every mutation parser must reject an unsupported suffix before returning a changed
database image. The malformed statements below used to execute their recognized
prefix and silently discard the rest.

[ByteSlice, SqliteValue, SqlInteger, SqlText, buildTableDatabase, buildTableWithIndexDatabase](std/scljet/index.ssc)
[executeMutationCountedParams](std/scljet/sql.ssc)

```scalascript
def reject(image: ByteSlice, label: String, sql: String): Unit =
  executeMutationCountedParams(image, sql, Nil) match
    case Left(message) => println(label + "=ERR:" + message)
    case Right(_) => println(label + "=UNSAFE-SUCCESS")

buildTableDatabase(512, 1, 1, "emp",
  "CREATE TABLE emp(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, note TEXT)",
  List(List(SqlInteger(1L), SqlText("seed")))) match
  case Left(error) => println("build-error:" + error.message)
  case Right(base) =>
    reject(base, "create-table-tail", "CREATE TABLE rogue(a INTEGER) garbage")
    reject(base, "create-table-missing-body", "CREATE TABLE rogue")
    reject(base, "create-table-unclosed", "CREATE TABLE rogue(a INTEGER")
    reject(base, "create-index-tail", "CREATE INDEX idx_bad ON emp(note) garbage")
    reject(base, "create-index-partial", "CREATE INDEX idx_bad ON emp(note) WHERE note = 'x'")
    reject(base, "bare-create", "CREATE")

buildTableWithIndexDatabase(512, 1, 1, "emp",
  "CREATE TABLE emp(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, note TEXT)",
  "idx_note", "CREATE INDEX idx_note ON emp(note)", List(1),
  List(List(SqlInteger(1L), SqlText("seed")))) match
  case Left(error) => println("indexed-build-error:" + error.message)
  case Right(base) =>
    reject(base, "drop-index-tail", "DROP INDEX idx_note garbage")
    reject(base, "bare-drop-index", "DROP INDEX")
```
